<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n46040" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑῷος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, <i><span class="en">
			A.
			<u>Pr.</u>
			25
		</span></i>, etc.; also <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ος</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>
		<i><span class="en">
			E.
			<u>Ph.</u>
			169
		</span></i> (lyr.), <i><span class="en">
			D.H.
			1.12
		</span></i>, dub. in <i><span class="en">
			Gem.
			<u>Calend.</u>
			p.220
		</span></i> M.: poet. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑώϊος</span></b> , 
			Ion.
		 and in <i><span class="en">
			Hom.
		</span></i>
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠοῖος</span></b>  (qq. v.): (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἕως</span> (A)):—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>in or of the morning</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πάχνην ἑ. ἥλιος σκεδᾷ</span> the <i>morning</i>
			rime, <i><span class="en">
				A.
			</span></i> l. c.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑ. φθέγματ᾽ ὀρνίθων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>El.</u>
					18
				</span></i>
			, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑ. ἀστήρ,</span>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἑωσφόρος</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				929
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Epigr.</u>
				15
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὔθ᾽ ἕσπερος οὔθ᾽ ἑ. οὕτω
					θαυμαστός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>EN</u>
					1129b28
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑ. ἐξαναστῆναι</span> to get up
				<i>early</i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>El.</u>
				786
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>eastern</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τεῖχος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>HG</u>
					4.4.9
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ ἑ</span>. <i>eastern
			parts</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Cont.</u>
				5
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξ ἑῴας</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χώρας</span>) <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				946b14
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατὰ τὰς ἑῴας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Mu.</u>
					394a11
				</span></i>
			 (perh. <i>in the morning</i>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>b.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑῴα, ἡ</span>,
				=
			<u>Oriens</u>, the <i>Eastern provinces</i> of the Roman
			Empire, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ τὴν ἑῴαν ἐπιτροπεύων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Philostr.
					<u>VS</u>
					2.1.13
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀρχὸς ἑῴας</span>,
			= Lat. <i>magister militum per Orientem,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				IG
				14.1073
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὕπαρχος ἑῴας</span>,
			= Lat. <i>praefectus praetorio Orientis,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				AP
				9.690
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(v A. D.)</span>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
